<%# THE INVENTORY COLUMN (Shop manual spec §7): the items, then Places and Suppliers. Every row is a
    view the index already serves — all items, `?low=1`, `?location=`, `?supplier=` — or the Places
    and Suppliers pages themselves. Places and Suppliers are one capped query each (ShellHelper), so
    the column costs the same however many there are.

    THE SCREEN'S "NEEDED BY A PROJECT" IS NOT THE TO BUY LIST, AND IS NOT HERE. It counts 20 of 20
    items, beside the Stock table's "Needed by" column: every item an open project's BOM names, a
    filter the index does not have. To buy (spec §9) is the few of those a project is short of, and
    it is a section at the top of the page itself, not a view of the stock to narrow to; a row of
    that name leading to it would name the wrong list. %>
<div class="column-group">
  <h2 class="column-head">Inventory</h2>
  <%= column_row "All items", inventory_items_path, key: [ :inventory_items ] %>
  <%= column_row "Low or out", inventory_items_path(low: 1), key: [ :low_stock ] %>
</div>
<div class="column-group">
  <h2 class="column-head">Places</h2>
  <% column_locations.each do |location| %>
    <%= column_row location.name, inventory_items_path(location: location.id), key: [ :location, location.id.to_s ] %>
  <% end %>
  <%= column_row "All places", locations_path, key: [ :locations ] %>
</div>
<div class="column-group">
  <h2 class="column-head">Suppliers</h2>
  <% column_suppliers.each do |supplier| %>
    <%= column_row supplier.name, inventory_items_path(supplier: supplier.id), key: [ :supplier, supplier.id.to_s ] %>
  <% end %>
  <%= column_row "All suppliers", suppliers_path, key: [ :suppliers ] %>
</div>
